1
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:30,160
They're meeting at Star Garden
to talk about the land.

2
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:31,840
You're sure it's that land?

3
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:35,040
Ten years ago, today,
or ten years from now,

4
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:37,080
I'll still love you the same.

5
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:38,760
You don't trust me anymore?

6
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:40,080
But I don't trust him.

7
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:42,280
I don't want you being close to him.

8
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:43,680
She was just transferred to the CSD,

9
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:45,040
and she's single too.

10
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:47,640
She hasn't handled any cases
involving influential figures.

11
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:50,240
I told you Fon could be trusted.
You just didn't believe me.

12
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:52,440
Then I'll give you one million more.

13
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:54,680
I'll let the other side
know your offer first.

14
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:56,240
You sure you can train?

15
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:58,640
I can, Oab.
If you send me back there to fight again,

16
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:01,120
I don't want to lose.

17
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:04,280
I got word from one of my sources.

18
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,880
Are you guys planning to go after Peng?

19
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:07,640
That means he probably knows by now.

20
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:10,160
Then set up a meeting
with the landowner. Tonight.

21
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:13,280
Tell him if he won't accept my offer,
I don't want the land anymore.

22
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:14,600
Drive for me, will you?

23
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:16,160
What about Pong? Isn't he coming?

24
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,680
I told him to wait there.

25
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:19,600
I already had our people waiting there.

26
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:21,360
<i>I'm setting a trap for him.</i>

27
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:23,960
<i>I'll have you and Dum take the money</i>
<i>to the landowner.</i>

28
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:26,280
<i>I think Peng will definitely send Liang.</i>

29
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,120
Dom and I
will go deal with Peng ourselves.

30
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:30,200
If Liang is with you, that means

31
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:31,800
Peng will have to go home alone.

32
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,040
Oab.

33
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:43,400
Hit him.

34
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:47,080
Oab!

35
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:48,600
Hey!

36
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:01,520
That's all you brought?

37
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:06,400
Is Oab in the car?

38
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:08,920
Why would he come?

39
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:10,920
I should be asking you that.

40
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,440
How could you leave Peng alone?

41
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:24,680
Want to know where Oab went?

42
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:27,880
He's meeting with your boss.

43
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:39,560
KING BOXING CAMP

44
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:41,200
How do you think Oab's doing?

45
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:43,200
I told you to meet him there,
but you didn't.

46
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:45,680
He told me
he was going to take care of Peng himself.

47
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:47,840
He said we should finish the job
and meet him here.

48
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:49,760
And you let him go with Dom alone?

49
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:53,400
Should I take some men and go after them?

50
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:54,680
No need, Dum.

51
00:04:55,280 --> 00:04:57,640
Oab, what happened?

52
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:03,640
Follow him.

53
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:15,960
You sneaky bastard!

54
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:17,040
Shoot me then.

55
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,840
- Don't.
- Do it. Come on!

56
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:19,920
- Don't. Stop.
- Go ahead!

57
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:23,680
I'll be able to have you arrested.
Come on.

58
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:25,480
Oab.

59
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:31,440
Let's go, Oab. Let's leave.

60
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:38,400
Go ahead.

61
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:51,520
They brought a whole bunch of people.

62
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:54,360
They were trying to take me out.

63
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:56,720
Good thing I'm hard to kill.

64
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:10,080
I think someone on our side
tipped them off.

65
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:16,480
I didn't know the glass was bulletproof.

66
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:17,920
Didn't your informant tell you?

67
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:20,240
No, he didn't.

68
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:22,080
It's fine.

69
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:26,200
He'll just be more careful from now on.

70
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:29,760
At least he'll know
we're not to be messed with.

71
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:30,720
For sure.

72
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:32,640
Oab was about to shoot Peng
at the station.

73
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:35,160
Oab!

74
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:36,320
I didn't shoot him.

75
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:40,280
I don't think he'll let this go.
A guy like him

76
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:41,840
won't just sit back and take it.

77
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,960
I know. I've already thought about it.

78
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:51,160
Tell our informant to stay put for now.
I can wait.

79
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:54,640
I'm going to kill him anyway.

80
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:57,960
But right now, I can't become a suspect.

81
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,400
<i>You and Dum go make sure</i>
<i>everyone's story matches.</i>

82
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:03,160
<i>If the police ask,</i>
<i>stick to the same answer.</i>

83
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:04,280
<i>And you, Dom.</i>

84
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:06,480
<i>Pack your things. You're coming with me.</i>

85
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:07,800
Right now?

86
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:09,000
Yeah.

87
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:13,240
Then wait a moment. I'll pack my bag.

88
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:29,160
Open the trunk.

89
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:53,560
You're taking Fon with us?

90
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,600
We need a witness
to confirm where we were tonight.

91
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:58,120
Where are we going?

92
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,280
Khon Kaen.

93
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:21,200
Let's go.

94
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:02,840
- Oh, is that you, Oab?
- Hello, Dad.

95
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:05,480
Dad.

96
00:09:05,560 --> 00:09:08,480
- Fon, come here.
- Who is it?

97
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:10,520
It's me, Mom.

98
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:12,600
I missed you so much.

99
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:15,480
I missed you.

100
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,760
She came with Oab.

101
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:18,440
- Hello.
- Hello.

102
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:21,040
How have you been?

103
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:22,720
I'm good. How about you, Oab?

104
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:23,880
I'm good.

105
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:25,080
I've gained a little weight.

106
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:31,520
Who drove you here?

107
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:35,480
Uh, one of my men.

108
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:51,040
Why don't you get out of the car?

109
00:09:53,680 --> 00:09:57,200
Come on. It must be hot in there.

110
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:04,080
It's Dom, Mom. Do you remember him?

111
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:07,160
The boxer from the temple fairs.

112
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:17,000
I remember.

113
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:22,400
The boxer who fought at temple fairs
to earn money.

114
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:33,320
Come on, it's hot.
Why are we standing out here talking?

115
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:34,680
Let's talk inside.

116
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:36,120
- Okay.
- Come on.

117
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:38,640
What are you making for dinner today?

118
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:40,800
Oh, lots of things.

119
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:42,040
I was about to go to the market.

120
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:45,320
- Really? Want me to go with you?
- No, you should rest.

121
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:58,640
So you're only staying for the weekend?

122
00:11:58,720 --> 00:11:59,680
Yes, Dad.

123
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:01,360
Oab invited me to come visit you and Mom.

124
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:06,400
Why don't you stay at Fon's house?

125
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:11,880
Wait. She doesn't live here?

126
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:14,560
This house is too far from her workplace.

127
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:17,040
I built another one
closer to where she works.

128
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:18,880
So she doesn't have to wake up early.

129
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:24,200
Then let's eat first,
and after that, have Fon take you there.

130
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:26,280
Sure.

131
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:32,280
I'll help.

132
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:33,800
Huh?

133
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:36,160
Oab, no need.

134
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:37,640
Sit and talk with me.

135
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:39,560
Let Fon and your man help Mom.

136
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:40,600
Okay.

137
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:41,800
Tell me.

138
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:43,440
How did you meet Fon?

139
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:46,680
It was such a coincidence.

140
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:53,640
He can't sleep at that house, Mom.

141
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:55,440
He'll just have to.

142
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:59,920
You know about this too?

143
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:02,520
I called Champ before we left.

144
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:04,920
Then wait a moment. I'll pack my bag.

145
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:23,480
Oab invited me to come home.
He's waiting outside my room right now.

146
00:13:29,040 --> 00:13:31,600
Sir, Oab is going to Fon's house.

147
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:32,960
I'll handle it.

148
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:35,320
Just make sure
you get there before they do.

149
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:36,680
Yes, sir.

150
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:41,000
Okay.

151
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:46,240
Honey, Fon and Dom will come with Oab
tomorrow morning.

152
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:48,720
We have to pretend we don't know Dom.

153
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:54,480
Dom, how much longer
are you going to keep doing this?

154
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:02,440
Until we catch Oab selling drugs, Mom.

155
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:07,280
Any sign of that happening?

156
00:14:09,440 --> 00:14:10,320
No, not at all.

157
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:14,360
I've never seen him
involved with drugs even once.

158
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:20,000
What if he's not involved with drugs?

159
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:24,520
Then the deal we made is over.

160
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:27,800
And I get nothing.

161
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:30,960
So you risked your life for nothing?

162
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:49,160
You tipped them off about me?

163
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:52,720
No, Boss.

164
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:57,720
You're trying to make excuses? Huh?

165
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:09,800
Have someone clean this up.

166
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:10,960
Yes.

167
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:14,880
What about you? Did you find out

168
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:16,360
where they are?

169
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:20,560
I heard Pong is in Bangkok,

170
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:23,000
but Oab and the others went out of town.

171
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:28,800
They came after me and ran away.

172
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:30,760
They think they'll get away?

173
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:52,600
Take care of him. Leave no trace.

174
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:58,680
Liang.

175
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:08,280
Someone wants you to join them.

176
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:10,280
Who?

177
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:12,000
Oab.

178
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:21,080
He wants to know what you want
if you have to work for him.

179
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:28,120
What I want,

180
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:30,680
he can't give me that.

181
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:43,040
You're the one
who bought off my guy, aren't you?

182
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:45,360
You called me here just to ask that?

183
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:51,080
Lucky I didn't call you here to kill you.

184
00:16:51,160 --> 00:16:53,240
So you wanted to talk.

185
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:56,240
What do you want?

186
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:00,560
Stay out of my way.

187
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:03,400
You can't give me what I want.

188
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:05,640
Try telling me first.

189
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:09,240
What do you want?

190
00:17:13,079 --> 00:17:15,440
I want to sell drugs
in your boss's territory.

191
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:21,200
Will you let me?

192
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:55,520
Fon is taking a huge risk.
Do you realize that?

193
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:58,000
Yes, I do.

194
00:17:58,080 --> 00:17:59,720
Why do you keep dragging her into trouble?

195
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:03,880
Fon went to Bangkok to advance her career.

196
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:07,080
But you're holding her back.

197
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:09,520
Now she has to put herself in danger

198
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:14,760
because you're being selfish
and want a stable career.

199
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:18,160
Have you ever thought

200
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:21,280
that she could have a better life
without you?

201
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:23,560
If you never have,

202
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:25,960
start thinking about it now.

203
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:28,160
And if you do realize that,

204
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:30,440
then break up with her.

205
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:57,640
I've been meaning to come by for a while.

206
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:58,720
Everything looks delicious, Mom.

207
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:00,240
It all looks delicious. Here.

208
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:02,000
- This is your favorite.
- Your cooking is still amazing.

209
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:06,840
This is your favorite too.
Go ahead, eat plenty.

210
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:08,000
- Yes.
- Hey, Dom.

211
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:10,760
Come eat with us.

212
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:13,600
Come on, we're waiting for you.
I'm starving.

213
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:16,640
I'll just take my food
and eat in the back.

214
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,880
Sure, you can eat in the back.

215
00:19:27,080 --> 00:19:28,560
Sit and eat with us.

216
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:29,880
Yeah.

217
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:32,280
Come eat with us.
Why eat back there by yourself?

218
00:19:32,360 --> 00:19:33,400
Come on.

219
00:19:35,520 --> 00:19:36,960
Alright.

220
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:41,040
Let's eat. I'm hungry.

221
00:20:18,320 --> 00:20:19,160
Fon.

222
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:22,440
Go sit and talk with Oab.

223
00:20:23,360 --> 00:20:25,080
I'll help Dom with the dishes.

224
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:46,120
You did this because you love Fon,
didn't you?

225
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,120
Yes, Mom.

226
00:20:55,640 --> 00:20:57,360
I never wanted it to be like this.

227
00:20:58,520 --> 00:21:00,680
I never wanted to put her life at risk.

228
00:21:02,120 --> 00:21:03,120
I'm sorry.

229
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:06,600
Don't apologize.

230
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:09,200
I'm rooting for you.

231
00:21:09,960 --> 00:21:12,440
I hope everything works out.

232
00:21:14,520 --> 00:21:15,640
Even a dirty dish

233
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:18,600
can be washed until it's clean again.

234
00:21:22,120 --> 00:21:25,280
People can start over too.

235
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:28,160
Dom.

236
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:30,760
I'm leaving Fon in your care.

237
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:42,520
I believe

238
00:21:44,080 --> 00:21:45,440
you can pull this off.

239
00:21:47,360 --> 00:21:50,400
Please protect your own life
for Fon's sake.

240
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:53,520
If anything happens,

241
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:56,320
protect her, okay?

242
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:09,280
Yes, Mom. I'll protect her

243
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:11,680
with my life.

244
00:22:35,320 --> 00:22:36,680
Where were you last night?

245
00:22:36,760 --> 00:22:38,160
I was right here at the camp.

246
00:22:38,800 --> 00:22:40,600
I was sitting there drinking beer.

247
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:47,520
- What about Mr. Oab?
- He went out with one of his men.

248
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:48,960
Why?

249
00:22:49,720 --> 00:22:52,280
I don't know.
You'll have to ask him yourself.

250
00:22:52,360 --> 00:22:53,560
When will he be back?

251
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:55,480
I really don't know.

252
00:22:55,560 --> 00:22:56,640
You'll have to ask him yourself.

253
00:23:02,920 --> 00:23:04,120
That's all, right?

254
00:23:05,040 --> 00:23:06,560
- I'll be leaving now.
- Yes.

255
00:23:06,640 --> 00:23:07,520
Goodbye.

256
00:23:09,360 --> 00:23:11,720
Why do they keep asking
the same questions?

257
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:13,920
Probably no evidence.

258
00:23:15,240 --> 00:23:17,200
Otherwise, they'd already have a warrant.

259
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:26,760
Mom, what about the things inside?

260
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:29,520
Fon, do you live here alone?

261
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:33,400
Yes.

262
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:44,200
No one's been here since Fon moved
to Bangkok. It must be dusty.

263
00:23:44,280 --> 00:23:46,240
We'll probably have to clean
everything again.

264
00:23:46,320 --> 00:23:48,680
I think you and Fon
should go to the other house first.

265
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:50,360
I'll clean up and come get you.

266
00:23:51,080 --> 00:23:54,760
That might be better. It's probably dusty.
It's been empty for so long.

267
00:23:56,360 --> 00:23:59,240
We'll do it together.
It won't take long. Come on.

268
00:24:00,520 --> 00:24:01,360
Oab!

269
00:24:32,920 --> 00:24:34,320
This house is really nice.

270
00:24:35,840 --> 00:24:38,160
It's just the right size for a family.

271
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:42,440
If you need anything, call us, okay?

272
00:24:42,520 --> 00:24:45,400
We'll get some things from the market
and leave them here for you,

273
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:46,440
so you don't have to go out.

274
00:24:46,520 --> 00:24:47,880
I can go with Fon.

275
00:24:49,560 --> 00:24:51,760
You just got here.
Why go to the market? It's hot.

276
00:24:51,840 --> 00:24:53,560
- Yeah.
- We have to go anyway.

277
00:24:53,640 --> 00:24:56,000
We'll pick up some things for you.

278
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:59,720
The three of you drove all this way,
so get some rest.

279
00:25:00,600 --> 00:25:02,480
- Yeah.
- Okay.

280
00:25:02,560 --> 00:25:05,160
Then we'll head out.
We'll drop some things off later.

281
00:25:05,760 --> 00:25:07,000
- Thank you.
- No problem.

282
00:25:07,840 --> 00:25:08,920
Bye.

283
00:26:08,080 --> 00:26:09,440
Hey, Dom.

284
00:26:10,040 --> 00:26:11,920
Go get some cleaning supplies.
I'll help you.

285
00:26:13,960 --> 00:26:15,120
I'll show you.

286
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:18,560
Okay.

287
00:26:59,120 --> 00:27:00,600
At first, I was so worried.

288
00:27:00,680 --> 00:27:02,840
When your parents had us stay here,
I thought I was screwed.

289
00:27:03,560 --> 00:27:05,440
I was surprised too.

290
00:27:05,520 --> 00:27:07,920
I wondered why my parents
weren't surprised at all.

291
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:11,120
Who came and packed everything?

292
00:27:11,920 --> 00:27:13,040
I don't know either.

293
00:27:14,880 --> 00:27:16,520
Dom.

294
00:27:16,600 --> 00:27:18,720
I want this to be over soon.

295
00:27:21,600 --> 00:27:22,880
Me too.

296
00:28:58,320 --> 00:28:59,480
Fon, Oab is coming.

297
00:29:11,840 --> 00:29:13,080
Oh, crap!

298
00:29:13,160 --> 00:29:15,520
Ouch. Whoa!

299
00:29:15,600 --> 00:29:19,040
- Hey.
- I'm fine. Just looking for something.

300
00:29:19,120 --> 00:29:20,560
Damn, everything fell over.

301
00:29:22,000 --> 00:29:23,720
Alright, it's okay. I'll clean it up.

302
00:29:23,800 --> 00:29:27,040
- Here. No, I'm fine. Come on.
- You're not hurt, are you?

303
00:29:27,120 --> 00:29:28,400
Damn it.

304
00:29:41,760 --> 00:29:44,520
Dom, sit down. I'll do it.
It'll only take a second.

305
00:29:44,600 --> 00:29:45,560
Give it to me. I'll sweep.

306
00:29:45,640 --> 00:29:47,320
You go get some water to mop the floor.

307
00:29:49,360 --> 00:29:51,280
Why are you acting so formal?

308
00:29:51,840 --> 00:29:53,080
Let's do it together. It'll be faster.

309
00:30:37,600 --> 00:30:39,720
Why didn't you tell me?
I could've helped carry them.

310
00:30:39,800 --> 00:30:41,200
It's not much. I can handle it.

311
00:30:52,800 --> 00:30:53,840
Come on.

312
00:30:57,720 --> 00:30:59,920
Go inside. I'll take care of it.

313
00:31:23,560 --> 00:31:24,680
Who is it?

314
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:32,600
Shit, a thief!

315
00:31:33,960 --> 00:31:34,880
Who are you?

316
00:31:35,480 --> 00:31:36,920
It's George.

317
00:31:39,760 --> 00:31:41,480
- I'm not a thief.
- You are.

318
00:31:41,560 --> 00:31:44,440
You really are.
Reminds me of when I was inside.

319
00:31:46,400 --> 00:31:48,280
Honestly,
I don't want to go back in there.

320
00:31:52,760 --> 00:31:53,840
- Listen to me first.
- Easy.

321
00:31:53,920 --> 00:31:55,320
That was weak.

322
00:31:56,440 --> 00:31:57,800
Wanna keep going?

323
00:32:03,920 --> 00:32:07,280
Felt like a feather.
You throwing cotton balls at me?

324
00:32:08,360 --> 00:32:09,960
You know the four-point punch?

325
00:32:11,160 --> 00:32:12,040
The four-point punch.

326
00:32:13,080 --> 00:32:15,320
One, two, three, four.
That could kill someone.

327
00:32:15,840 --> 00:32:16,680
You ready?

328
00:32:18,760 --> 00:32:19,880
Oab!

329
00:32:21,840 --> 00:32:22,800
He's my friend.

330
00:32:26,760 --> 00:32:28,000
Well…

331
00:32:28,080 --> 00:32:30,960
I was trying to tell him I'm not a thief.

332
00:32:31,040 --> 00:32:33,160
If you're not, then you're not.

333
00:32:34,560 --> 00:32:36,680
Enough.

334
00:32:43,560 --> 00:32:45,600
What are you doing here? Huh?

335
00:32:45,680 --> 00:32:48,680
There was a boxing match
at the temple fair in the next district,

336
00:32:48,760 --> 00:32:52,720
so I came to see if you were around.
I saw the car here, so I rang the bell.

337
00:32:52,800 --> 00:32:55,320
Then I ran into that ugly guy.

338
00:32:55,400 --> 00:32:56,560
I thought he was a thief.

339
00:32:57,440 --> 00:32:58,280
That's my boss.

340
00:32:58,360 --> 00:33:00,280
- Your boss?
- Yeah.

341
00:33:00,360 --> 00:33:01,920
Good thing you saved him.

342
00:33:11,400 --> 00:33:13,600
By the way,
what were you doing in Bangkok?

343
00:33:13,680 --> 00:33:15,160
Just doing odd jobs.

344
00:33:20,360 --> 00:33:22,520
Hey, I don't think I'll go.

345
00:33:22,600 --> 00:33:24,480
Let's skip this one for now
and talk later.

346
00:33:24,560 --> 00:33:27,040
The new promoter
brought a lot of fighters.

347
00:33:27,120 --> 00:33:29,600
- You'd win for sure. Not interested?
- No.

348
00:33:30,240 --> 00:33:31,640
Go home. Leave!

349
00:33:31,720 --> 00:33:34,800
How about this? I'll be at Ban Phai Temple
in case you change your mind, okay?

350
00:33:34,880 --> 00:33:36,320
- Leave.
- Just go back.

351
00:33:41,520 --> 00:33:42,560
That was close.

352
00:33:43,200 --> 00:33:45,480
We shouldn't stay here long.
It's too risky.

353
00:34:00,480 --> 00:34:01,440
Who was that guy?

354
00:34:12,880 --> 00:34:13,760
He's a temple boy.

355
00:34:20,239 --> 00:34:21,080
He's your friend?

356
00:34:21,880 --> 00:34:24,520
Yeah. He's a temple boy.

357
00:34:25,159 --> 00:34:27,199
My mom often goes to the temple
to make merit,

358
00:34:27,280 --> 00:34:28,920
so I know George.

359
00:34:37,000 --> 00:34:38,360
But he knows Dom too.

360
00:34:48,239 --> 00:34:50,480
Fon didn't know George knew me either.

361
00:34:52,320 --> 00:34:55,639
Yeah. He saw someone was at the house,

362
00:34:55,719 --> 00:34:56,920
so he invited me to make merit.

363
00:34:58,240 --> 00:35:01,280
He was probably surprised
to see me here too.

364
00:35:06,120 --> 00:35:07,000
What were you guys talking about?

365
00:35:12,120 --> 00:35:13,920
I usually train boxing with him.

366
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:16,200
When he saw me,
he invited me to a boxing match.

367
00:35:16,280 --> 00:35:18,680
The district next door
is having a temple fair.

368
00:35:33,440 --> 00:35:35,080
I'll put the water away.

369
00:35:35,880 --> 00:35:37,080
- I'll help.
- It's okay.

370
00:36:04,120 --> 00:36:07,280
Just looking for something.
Damn, everything fell over.

371
00:36:09,560 --> 00:36:11,320
Alright, it's okay. I'll clean it up.

372
00:37:11,160 --> 00:37:13,360
You left your hair tie
in the storage room.

373
00:37:15,640 --> 00:37:18,240
It probably fell off
while I was looking for supplies.

374
00:37:18,800 --> 00:37:19,680
I didn't notice.

375
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:23,080
Here.

376
00:37:24,320 --> 00:37:25,160
Thank you.

377
00:37:25,240 --> 00:37:26,480
No problem.

378
00:37:28,280 --> 00:37:30,800
Since we're here anyway,
why don't we go out after this?

379
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:33,400
Is that a good idea?

380
00:37:34,800 --> 00:37:38,600
Why not? I didn't bring any clothes,
so I need to go buy some.

381
00:37:42,480 --> 00:37:44,840
- Yes.
- What's wrong?

382
00:37:44,920 --> 00:37:49,200
Well, I don't know if there are
any of Peng's guys around here.

383
00:37:51,800 --> 00:37:52,960
Are you afraid of him?

384
00:38:02,160 --> 00:38:03,960
I've already taken care of the house.

385
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:14,520
Yes, I'll keep an eye on things.

386
00:38:20,160 --> 00:38:21,960
When did he leave this here?

387
00:38:22,680 --> 00:38:25,800
He left it in front of the camp.
The fighters saw it on their run.

388
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:27,960
Damn it.

389
00:38:28,560 --> 00:38:29,840
So Liang's not joining us.

390
00:38:29,920 --> 00:38:31,840
If we can't get him on our side,

391
00:38:32,360 --> 00:38:34,000
taking Peng down won't be easy.

392
00:38:38,520 --> 00:38:40,320
Hey, take it away.

393
00:38:56,080 --> 00:38:57,160
- What the hell?
- Hey!

394
00:39:02,840 --> 00:39:04,520
‪-Whoa! What the hell?
‪-Hey!

395
00:39:05,600 --> 00:39:07,680
What's going on? Pong!

396
00:39:07,760 --> 00:39:09,840
- Hey! Pong!
- Stop right there!

397
00:39:09,920 --> 00:39:11,320
Who the hell are they?

398
00:39:14,160 --> 00:39:15,840
A miracle? My ass.

399
00:39:15,920 --> 00:39:16,880
I'm just smart.

400
00:39:18,120 --> 00:39:20,960
The headline makes it sound
like magic saved me.

401
00:39:25,320 --> 00:39:27,920
Did you deliver my love letter to them?

402
00:39:28,720 --> 00:39:29,480
Yes.

403
00:39:29,560 --> 00:39:30,640
Good.

404
00:39:31,520 --> 00:39:33,800
They'll know better than to mess with me.

405
00:39:34,440 --> 00:39:36,240
If you find their mole,

406
00:39:36,320 --> 00:39:37,560
kill them.

407
00:39:39,920 --> 00:39:41,520
I don't tolerate disobedient dogs.

408
00:39:50,280 --> 00:39:51,400
Who the hell are you?

409
00:39:51,480 --> 00:39:52,600
Damn!

410
00:40:00,040 --> 00:40:01,320
Come on.

411
00:40:07,600 --> 00:40:09,040
What's with the attitude?

412
00:40:10,520 --> 00:40:11,840
I thought it was someone else.

413
00:40:13,120 --> 00:40:16,200
If you wanted to see me,
you could've just called, Sir.

414
00:40:16,840 --> 00:40:18,920
You still have the nerve to call me that?

415
00:40:28,440 --> 00:40:31,000
You know Peng filed a complaint
against you, right?

416
00:40:31,800 --> 00:40:32,840
I know.

417
00:40:33,520 --> 00:40:35,640
He said it was your people who did it.

418
00:40:36,360 --> 00:40:37,360
Where's Oab?

419
00:40:40,760 --> 00:40:42,840
- You're smiling?
- We didn't do it.

420
00:40:43,600 --> 00:40:46,000
What am I supposed to say?
Does he have any evidence?

421
00:40:50,080 --> 00:40:51,520
Do you know

422
00:40:51,600 --> 00:40:54,880
how easy it would've been
to take you and your guys?

423
00:40:58,800 --> 00:41:00,240
Where's Oab?

424
00:41:04,080 --> 00:41:05,800
He went to Khon Kaen.

425
00:41:06,680 --> 00:41:07,720
When?

426
00:41:11,160 --> 00:41:12,400
Yesterday evening.

427
00:41:13,400 --> 00:41:16,400
That was before Peng came to the station.

428
00:41:18,720 --> 00:41:19,840
Why did he go?

429
00:41:21,880 --> 00:41:24,520
I don't know. He didn't tell me.

430
00:41:28,360 --> 00:41:29,840
If he comes back,

431
00:41:30,880 --> 00:41:32,480
tell him to come see me.

432
00:41:53,480 --> 00:41:54,640
After you.

433
00:41:57,800 --> 00:41:59,040
Thank you.

434
00:42:01,320 --> 00:42:02,480
Come on.

435
00:42:03,640 --> 00:42:05,320
Dom, wait here. We'll be back in a bit.

436
00:42:21,600 --> 00:42:23,800
- Take it slow.
- Okay.

437
00:42:32,560 --> 00:42:33,480
Thank you.

438
00:42:37,800 --> 00:42:40,360
I don't remember the walk being this hard
when we were in school.

439
00:42:41,760 --> 00:42:43,000
Maybe we were just younger.

440
00:42:45,240 --> 00:42:49,160
Back then, skipping class to come here
was already fun enough.

441
00:42:51,600 --> 00:42:53,720
We didn't know where else to go,
so we came here.

442
00:43:14,120 --> 00:43:14,840
Come here.

443
00:43:16,840 --> 00:43:18,720
Come sit here.

444
00:43:23,280 --> 00:43:24,560
Sit down.

445
00:43:31,600 --> 00:43:34,560
Why did you bring me here?
We walked so far.

446
00:43:34,640 --> 00:43:37,040
It's Valentine's Day.

447
00:43:38,680 --> 00:43:41,320
- Yeah.
- Did you forget?

448
00:43:42,280 --> 00:43:45,040
Even if I did,
seeing all those stickers on your shirt

449
00:43:45,800 --> 00:43:47,600
would've reminded me.

450
00:43:50,080 --> 00:43:51,560
But I'm still waiting for yours.

451
00:43:53,480 --> 00:43:56,720
Your shirt is already covered.
You still want mine?

452
00:43:56,800 --> 00:44:01,000
I don't want the ones on my shirt.
I want yours.

453
00:44:23,200 --> 00:44:24,600
Will you be my girlfriend?

454
00:44:40,680 --> 00:44:42,320
You still remember?

455
00:44:44,000 --> 00:44:46,280
How could I forget?
I asked you to be my girlfriend here.

456
00:45:04,760 --> 00:45:07,600
I know I've been gone too long
to ask you this now.

457
00:45:11,600 --> 00:45:14,120
- I just want to say--
- But back then, you disappeared.

458
00:45:15,520 --> 00:45:18,040
You knew I was still at the same school,

459
00:45:18,680 --> 00:45:20,040
living in the same house,

460
00:45:21,000 --> 00:45:22,680
but you never contacted me.

461
00:45:52,560 --> 00:45:54,480
I didn't want you to see me struggling

462
00:45:56,080 --> 00:45:57,120
and unhappy.

463
00:46:01,280 --> 00:46:04,760
How could I take care of you?
How could I make you happy when…

464
00:46:06,120 --> 00:46:08,560
I could barely make myself happy
back then?

465
00:46:47,680 --> 00:46:49,120
I'm sorry.

466
00:46:54,080 --> 00:46:54,880
It's okay.

467
00:46:57,600 --> 00:47:00,280
If I were you, I'd feel the same way.

468
00:47:10,120 --> 00:47:11,560
But I was serious.

469
00:47:15,240 --> 00:47:18,920
I promised myself that when I had enough
to give you a comfortable life…

470
00:47:21,080 --> 00:47:22,400
I would come back to you.

471
00:47:52,720 --> 00:47:55,480
Hey! Why are you here?
Why didn't you park at the entrance?

472
00:47:55,560 --> 00:47:56,720
They'll find out.

473
00:47:59,560 --> 00:48:00,840
I came to check on you.

474
00:48:06,360 --> 00:48:07,480
Are you annoyed?

475
00:48:12,440 --> 00:48:14,200
Have some faith in Fon.

476
00:48:18,920 --> 00:48:21,320
So what? You're just going
to follow me around like this?

477
00:48:22,680 --> 00:48:25,160
Yeah. The chief ordered me to.

478
00:48:25,240 --> 00:48:28,920
I told you not to follow me.
If anything happens, I'll tell you myself.

479
00:48:34,440 --> 00:48:35,520
Hey.

480
00:48:35,600 --> 00:48:37,480
Thanks for helping clean up the house.

481
00:48:39,160 --> 00:48:40,280
Yeah.

482
00:48:41,000 --> 00:48:43,960
Can you clean it up properly next time?
He almost found out.

483
00:48:44,040 --> 00:48:45,360
You rascal.

484
00:48:46,240 --> 00:48:47,760
I only had a few hours.

485
00:48:48,320 --> 00:48:50,040
You're lucky I got it done in time.

486
00:48:52,040 --> 00:48:53,320
Thank you.

487
00:49:02,200 --> 00:49:04,400
Think about the day you become
a police boxer,

488
00:49:05,520 --> 00:49:08,400
with a rank, a career,

489
00:49:09,720 --> 00:49:10,960
and a salary.

490
00:49:14,600 --> 00:49:16,600
You might even make the Olympic team.

491
00:49:21,040 --> 00:49:22,120
Just be patient.

492
00:49:23,440 --> 00:49:24,880
It's only for now.

493
00:49:29,280 --> 00:49:30,480
I'm leaving.

494
00:49:45,000 --> 00:49:47,680
- Thank you.
- I'll open the gate for you.

495
00:49:49,400 --> 00:49:50,320
NO ENTRY

496
00:49:52,320 --> 00:49:54,240
- Come on.
- We're going home, right?

497
00:49:55,080 --> 00:49:55,920
No.

498
00:49:56,680 --> 00:49:57,840
Let's go to the temple fair.

499
00:49:58,680 --> 00:50:00,200
- The temple fair?
- Yeah.

500
00:50:00,280 --> 00:50:02,680
That guy we met said
there's a boxing match at the fair, right?

501
00:50:02,760 --> 00:50:06,760
It's risky. The place will be packed.
We don't know who's around. Let's not go.

502
00:50:09,760 --> 00:50:12,840
Seriously, are you two running away
from something?

503
00:50:13,560 --> 00:50:14,760
- No.
- No.

504
00:50:16,760 --> 00:50:19,440
Really? You answered at the same time.

505
00:50:24,160 --> 00:50:26,920
Well, there's just a little something
going on.

506
00:50:29,000 --> 00:50:32,720
I knew it. That's why you suddenly
wanted to come see my parents.

507
00:50:33,360 --> 00:50:36,160
I really did want to come.
It just happened to be a good opportunity.

508
00:50:36,240 --> 00:50:38,360
But I think we shouldn't go.

509
00:50:38,440 --> 00:50:39,800
Let's just go home.

510
00:50:44,920 --> 00:50:46,560
No, let's go.

511
00:50:47,640 --> 00:50:51,200
You're a boxer. There's a ring.
You have to fight.

512
00:50:54,000 --> 00:50:55,000
Let's go.

513
00:51:03,000 --> 00:51:04,320
Give it a shot.

514
00:51:54,840 --> 00:51:57,160
That car has been following us
since the waterfall.

515
00:52:00,440 --> 00:52:02,440
- Really?
- Yeah.

516
00:52:18,960 --> 00:52:20,200
Pull over at the gas station.

517
00:52:57,240 --> 00:52:58,320
Why are you following me?

518
00:53:02,720 --> 00:53:03,880
Sorry.

519
00:53:24,800 --> 00:53:25,840
That's not it.

520
00:53:31,640 --> 00:53:33,400
Oab, I'll go buy something from the store.

521
00:53:53,440 --> 00:53:56,000
Three hats, and this one too.
That'll be 70 baht.

522
00:54:29,120 --> 00:54:32,000
BAN PHAI TEMPLE

523
00:54:34,600 --> 00:54:36,520
Five o'clock.

524
00:54:36,600 --> 00:54:39,320
A big boxing match from Bangkok.

525
00:54:40,240 --> 00:54:41,760
Five o'clock.

526
00:54:41,840 --> 00:54:43,960
We still have over an hour.

527
00:54:45,320 --> 00:54:46,680
Fon, wanna go do something?

528
00:54:48,680 --> 00:54:49,400
Sure.

529
00:55:00,360 --> 00:55:01,360
Keep the change.

530
00:55:02,240 --> 00:55:04,640
- Here.
- Thanks.

531
00:55:06,560 --> 00:55:08,880
Oab, I'll go find George
by the stage first.

532
00:55:08,960 --> 00:55:10,320
Okay.

533
00:55:23,960 --> 00:55:25,560
Which one do you like?

534
00:55:26,240 --> 00:55:28,160
Just tell me. I'll scoop it for you.

535
00:55:34,720 --> 00:55:35,800
Then I'll take a goldfish.

536
00:55:37,080 --> 00:55:38,120
There are a lot of them.

537
00:55:45,240 --> 00:55:47,240
Oab, are you done yet?

538
00:55:47,840 --> 00:55:49,720
Come on, finish up. We're gonna miss it.

539
00:55:49,800 --> 00:55:51,680
- Alright, let's go.
- Okay.

540
00:55:54,760 --> 00:55:57,800
Fon, I'll meet you by the stage.

541
00:55:57,880 --> 00:56:00,600
What? I haven't caught a single one yet.

542
00:56:00,680 --> 00:56:03,920
I'll scoop one for you next time.
Arm's in a hurry today.

543
00:56:04,880 --> 00:56:06,840
How about this? I'll go save us a spot.

544
00:56:06,920 --> 00:56:08,040
Okay.

545
00:56:13,760 --> 00:56:16,360
- Got it!
- Wow!

546
00:56:16,440 --> 00:56:18,000
You always get one.

547
00:56:19,040 --> 00:56:20,840
- You never miss.
- You didn't get one?

548
00:56:21,680 --> 00:56:22,840
Can I have another scoop?

549
00:56:22,920 --> 00:56:24,160
I'll get one for you.

550
00:56:31,440 --> 00:56:33,120
He can't fight. There's no opponent.

551
00:56:33,200 --> 00:56:36,720
- Hey, is this rigged?
- My event. I'll run it however I want.

552
00:56:36,800 --> 00:56:40,960
It's fighters from Singto Thong facing
each other. Where's the fun in that?

553
00:56:41,040 --> 00:56:42,560
Hey, George. If they won't let me fight,
let's just go home.

554
00:56:42,640 --> 00:56:44,120
- Come on.
- No way!

555
00:56:44,200 --> 00:56:46,880
- They're not letting anyone fight.
- Come on, let's go.

556
00:56:46,960 --> 00:56:48,160
They're just after the betting money.

557
00:56:48,240 --> 00:56:49,960
You already know who's gonna win, right?

558
00:56:50,040 --> 00:56:51,760
It's basically like fixing a fight.

559
00:56:51,840 --> 00:56:53,080
Hey, they won't let you fight?

560
00:56:56,000 --> 00:56:57,360
Here.

561
00:56:57,440 --> 00:56:59,160
Take this. Keep it.

562
00:57:00,040 --> 00:57:02,400
And I'll give another 5,000 as a prize
for the winner.

563
00:57:11,640 --> 00:57:12,960
Are you sure it's him?

564
00:57:13,560 --> 00:57:15,240
Then take care of it for me.

565
00:57:20,720 --> 00:57:22,720
Koh said he saw Oab in Khon Kaen.

566
00:57:22,800 --> 00:57:25,200
He's probably looking for witnesses

567
00:57:25,280 --> 00:57:27,080
to prove they weren't the shooters.

568
00:57:27,160 --> 00:57:29,680
But this time,
I'm the one hunting them down.

569
00:57:36,200 --> 00:57:37,800
I'm going to win you over again.

570
00:57:40,560 --> 00:57:42,760
I'll make you feel the same way
about me again.

571
00:57:45,240 --> 00:57:48,720
Where did you sell them?
You ran out in less than a week.

572
00:57:48,800 --> 00:57:49,880
Around the gambling den.

573
00:57:49,960 --> 00:57:51,960
- Which one?
- Phetchaburi.

574
00:57:52,040 --> 00:57:53,600
That's Oab's territory.

575
00:57:56,520 --> 00:57:58,200
How about this? This time,

576
00:57:58,280 --> 00:58:00,680
I'll buy whatever you have.

577
00:58:00,760 --> 00:58:03,400
But you have to take me
to the person you got it from.

578
00:58:03,480 --> 00:58:04,640
Deal?

579
00:58:06,400 --> 00:58:08,480
What's the point
of having a hitman connection?

580
00:58:08,560 --> 00:58:10,680
I already took care
of his younger brother.

581
00:58:10,760 --> 00:58:13,040
Taking care of the older one
won't be hard either.

582
00:58:54,840 --> 00:58:55,880
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
